@tradition captains-address
// The Captain's Friday address (EW1's words, moved in by FR1 for Short Fridays, plans/fridays-build-brief.md turn 5):
// every Friday from Day 5, 16:00-16:50 in the rec deck auditorium, the day shift off at 15:30, dinner at 17:00. Its
// rules live in the game (section 18f's FRI_ADDRESS, like the rec deck's REC_TRADS): Marrow and Vance at the lectern,
// everyone else in the seats; the Friday skeleton (a helm and a watch rating, a medic, the galley) never; night shift
// half. This file brings its words; the rules below say the same, for the check. It's in the game only with
// SHORT_FRIDAY on. The speech itself: content/addresses/ (turn 6). The first week's Mail (Day 4, your first week) is
// content/banks/fridays.lines' fri.mail.week1.
k: 499
title: The Captain's Friday address
when: weekly friday from day 5
at: 16:00-16:50
min: 20
prio: 3
where: 7 pool rec:lectern
where: 7 pool rec-aud
hold: none
who: marrow always, vance always, night-shift 50%, everyone 90%
host: marrow
from: Captain Odile Marrow

== mail
- Tomorrow's a short Friday: the day shift stops at half past three. The Captain's address is at four in the rec deck auditorium. Dinner at five.

== ask
- Captain at four. Back row's mine. Don't tell anyone.   #funny
- Half three, clock out, then the auditorium. Coming?
- She always says one thing you remember all week. Come and hear it.   #warm

== here
- Shh. She's starting.
- Good turnout. She'll notice. She notices everything.
- Budge up. There's a seat by me.

== thanks
- You find a seat in the auditorium as Captain Marrow steps up to the lectern. Commander Vance stands beside her.

== chatter
- Did you hear the Captain's address? She named the galley again.   #warm
- "Those of you who have one." She says it every Friday. I wait for it.   #funny
- Best part of a Friday: half three. Second best: the Captain.
